<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47011" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŭprēmĭtas</span></b> ,
			ātis, f.
		supremus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the highest extreme</i> (late Lat.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The last of life</i>, <i>death</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sepultura, qui supremitatis ho nor est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 31, 13, 17</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The highest honor</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">supremitates et praeeminentias adire,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. Mam. Stat. Anim. 2, 13</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
